1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,900
Imagine you're driving on a highway, a toll plaza comes
up, and you pass through without stopping.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,333
Within seconds, an SMS arrives on your phone
saying the toll has been deducted.

3
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:17,067
But with no cash, no card and no stopping, how
was the money deducted?

4
00:00:18,333 --> 00:00:20,833
What does this small sticker on your
windshield actually do?

5
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,100
Today, let's understand the technology behind
FASTag, step by step.

6
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:33,100
First, let's understand what FASTag actually
is.

7
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:37,767
FASTag is a small RFID sticker that is fixed
on the vehicle's windshield.

8
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:42,067
It links your vehicle to a prepaid wallet or a
bank account.

9
00:00:42,767 --> 00:00:46,600
Its job is to pay the toll automatically,
without stopping at the toll plaza.

10
00:00:47,233 --> 00:00:51,600
FASTag is part of the National Electronic Toll
Collection, or NETC, programme.

11
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:57,367
The NETC system was developed by NPCI, the
same NPCI that runs UPI.

12
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:02,600
In India, FASTag was made mandatory for most
vehicles from February 2021.

13
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:06,367
Queues got shorter, and the cash hassle went
away.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,433
To get a FASTag, you need the vehicle's RC and
KYC documents.

15
00:01:14,133 --> 00:01:17,267
Let's first understand the main parts of the
FASTag system.

16
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:22,933
First, the FASTag itself, with a unique Tag
ID.

17
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:27,233
Second is the toll plaza's RFID reader and
antenna, fixed above the lane.

18
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:32,433
Third is the toll plaza's computer system,
which handles the data of every lane.

19
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:36,900
Fourth is the acquirer bank, the bank that
collects payment on behalf of the toll plaza.

20
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,667
Fifth is the issuer bank, the bank that issued
your FASTag and holds your wallet.

21
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:47,367
And between them all is NPCI's NETC system,
which routes messages to the right bank.

22
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:54,833
Different banks issue FASTags, but thanks to NETC, your
tag works at every FASTag toll plaza in India.

23
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:03,233
Now the most interesting question. This small
sticker has no battery, so how does it work?

24
00:02:03,667 --> 00:02:08,600
FASTag uses RFID technology, which means Radio
Frequency Identification.

25
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:12,933
Inside the sticker there is a tiny chip, with
a thin antenna around it.

26
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:18,933
When the vehicle comes near the reader, the
reader sends out radio waves.

27
00:02:19,467 --> 00:02:23,100
These radio waves give the tag's chip a little
energy, and it becomes active.

28
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:28,667
The tag then sends its unique ID back to the
reader as a radio signal.

29
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:34,933
This is called passive RFID, so FASTag needs
no battery or charging.

30
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:38,567
Note that your money or bank details are not
stored inside the tag.

31
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:44,833
The tag only tells its ID; all the other work happens on
the servers of the banks and the NETC system.

32
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:51,100
In India, FASTag works on a UHF radio frequency band, so the
reader can read the tag from a few metres away.

33
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:58,300
If the sticker gets bent or torn, its antenna can be
damaged, and the reader may not be able to read it.

34
00:03:00,867 --> 00:03:04,133
Now let's see what actually happens at the
toll plaza, step by step.

35
00:03:04,367 --> 00:03:09,267
Suppose your FASTag wallet has five hundred
rupees, and the toll is ninety-five rupees.

36
00:03:09,967 --> 00:03:13,867
As soon as the car enters the FASTag lane, the
reader reads the tag's ID.

37
00:03:14,967 --> 00:03:18,800
The toll plaza system uses this ID to check
the tag's details and status.

38
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:23,500
The plaza keeps an updated status list of
tags, so the check can happen very quickly.

39
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:30,067
If the tag is valid, the toll amount is set by
the vehicle's class, and the barrier opens.

40
00:03:31,567 --> 00:03:34,633
Then the toll plaza sends the transaction to
its acquirer bank.

41
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:41,000
The acquirer bank passes this request to your
issuer bank through NPCI's NETC system.

42
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:45,800
The issuer bank debits ninety-five rupees from
your FASTag wallet.

43
00:03:48,167 --> 00:03:51,900
After that, through settlement, the money
reaches the toll plaza's account.

44
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:55,467
And a debit SMS arrives on your phone.

45
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:00,933
Note that the barrier can open immediately, but the
debit SMS may sometimes come a little later.

46
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:06,533
At many toll plazas, cameras also check the
vehicle's number plate and class.

47
00:04:07,433 --> 00:04:10,767
And this whole process is usually completed in
just a few seconds.

48
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:15,200
Now the question is, how is the toll amount
decided?

49
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:20,500
Every FASTag is linked to a vehicle class, like car,
light commercial vehicle, bus or truck.

50
00:04:21,133 --> 00:04:24,833
Every toll plaza has its own fee rate, which
differs by vehicle class.

51
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:28,067
That's why a truck pays more toll than a car.

52
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:33,000
Many plazas may also offer options like return
journey or monthly passes.

53
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:37,333
If you are ever charged for the wrong class,
you can complain to your issuer bank.

54
00:04:37,367 --> 00:04:40,833
Toll rates are updated from time to time, as
per government rules.

55
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:47,433
Every toll plaza's fee rate can be checked on
NHAI's official website or app.

56
00:04:50,733 --> 00:04:54,833
Sometimes a vehicle gets stopped at the toll
plaza even with a FASTag. Why?

57
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,333
The most common reason is low balance.

58
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:03,233
If the wallet doesn't have enough balance, the tag can
go into low-balance or blacklist status.

59
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:08,400
Incomplete KYC, or vehicle details that don't
match, can also be a reason.

60
00:05:08,633 --> 00:05:14,300
Under the One Vehicle One FASTag policy of NHAI, a
vehicle should have only one active FASTag.

61
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:18,700
Without a valid FASTag, you may have to pay
more than the normal toll.

62
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,233
So check your balance and tag status before a
trip.

63
00:05:23,167 --> 00:05:26,933
After you recharge, the tag's status becomes
active again within some time.

64
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:31,200
Now, let's talk about recharging your FASTag.

65
00:05:31,467 --> 00:05:35,167
Most FASTags work like a prepaid wallet that
you recharge in advance.

66
00:05:36,733 --> 00:05:41,467
You can recharge through the issuer bank's
app, net banking, or UPI payment apps.

67
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:46,467
Some banks also give the option to link FASTag
directly to your bank account.

68
00:05:46,833 --> 00:05:50,867
After a recharge, the balance can sometimes
take a little time to update.

69
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,433
So before a long journey, it's better to
recharge a little in advance.

70
00:05:54,867 --> 00:05:57,733
Many banks also send an SMS alert when the
balance is low.

71
00:05:58,667 --> 00:06:03,800
Some apps also have an auto-recharge option, which tops up
the wallet as soon as the balance runs low.

72
00:06:05,667 --> 00:06:08,000
Got a FASTag problem? Here's what to do.

73
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:12,533
Sometimes the tag is not read, because it's
damaged or fixed in the wrong place.

74
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:17,567
FASTag should be fixed on the windshield,
behind the rear-view mirror, in the centre.

75
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:21,800
Sometimes the same toll is deducted twice, or
a wrong amount is deducted.

76
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:27,067
In that case, keep the SMS and transaction
details, and complain to your issuer bank.

77
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:32,167
For highway-related help, there is also NHAI's
helpline number, 1033.

78
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:36,833
After checking, if the deduction is found to
be wrong, you can get a refund.

79
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:41,833
When you complain, be sure to mention the vehicle
number, date, time and toll plaza name.

80
00:06:43,733 --> 00:06:47,133
FASTag is safe, but it's important to keep a
few things in mind.

81
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:49,867
Buy FASTag only from a bank or an official
app.

82
00:06:50,733 --> 00:06:54,900
Never share your OTP or PIN on calls or links
about FASTag or KYC.

83
00:06:56,267 --> 00:07:00,800
Don't remove the tag and stick it on another vehicle,
because a tag is for one vehicle only.

84
00:07:00,967 --> 00:07:03,467
Selling your car? Close the old FASTag.

85
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:08,267
And always keep SMS alerts on, so you know
about every deduction.

86
00:07:10,067 --> 00:07:15,133
If your FASTag is lost or stolen, inform your issuer
bank right away and get the tag blocked.

87
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,667
In future, toll collection is going to get
even smarter.

88
00:07:19,867 --> 00:07:25,900
Work is going on on satellite or GNSS-based tolling, where
toll could be charged by the distance travelled.

89
00:07:26,433 --> 00:07:29,700
Cameras that recognise number plates can also
make this system faster.

90
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:38,100
So, to recap: the reader reads your tag's ID, the plaza
system checks the status, and the barrier opens.

91
00:07:39,133 --> 00:07:44,767
Then the acquirer bank, the NETC system and the issuer
bank together debit the toll from your wallet.

92
00:07:45,033 --> 00:07:48,267
A small sticker is really the story of a big
connected payment network.

93
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,900
If you enjoy understanding the systems behind technology,
please like this video and subscribe to the channel.

94
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:58,167
See you in the next video. Thank you!
